 "session_ne": "दोस्रो",
 "summary": "The name of this bill is Good Governance (Management and Operation) (First Amendment) Act, 2083 (Section 1, Subsection 1, Page 5). The main purpose of this bill is to amend the Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 to make provisions enabling the Government of Nepal to make and implement necessary rules, guidelines, procedures, standards, norms, guidance, and manuals for the effective implementation of the Act and to make the operations of government offices systematic, prompt, and economical while maintaining uniformity and fixed standards in work procedures (Statement of Objects and Reasons, Page 1). This Act shall come into force immediately (Section 1, Subsection 2, Page 5).\n\nThe Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers may make delegated legislation, including necessary rules, guidelines, procedures, standards, norms, and guidance to implement this Act (Section 2, Subsection 1, Page 5). A Ministry may make and implement internal manuals as necessary to conduct operations or perform work procedurally, promptly, and economically (Section 2, Subsection 2, Page 5). Regarding provincial and local governments, it is not stated in the bill.\n\nThis bill repeals Section 45 of the principal Act (Section 3, Page 5). What happens to staff, assets, and funds is not stated in the bill.",
